{# Markdown speech contract (2026-09-24): assistant prose renders through a
   markdown renderer (Streamdown) on every chat surface — the model must KNOW
   its message is markdown, or it improvises literal '•' bullets and glued
   lines (the capability-answer formatting collapse that birthed this law:
   enumeration items fused into one paragraph because they were not markdown
   list lines). One definition, three consumers (intent_router_system /
   chat_intent_system / trigger_system SPEECH blocks). #}MARKDOWN: your message renders as markdown — write it as markdown. '- ' bullet lines for enumerations: ONE item per line, a blank line before the list. **bold** for a group label or a key term. Never literal '•' / '–' bullets, never two items crammed onto one line. Plain sentences stay plain — markdown carries structure, never decoration: no headings (#), no horizontal rules, no code blocks unless the user asked for code.
